c Wireless activation patterns on a 6 by 6 grid of sites.
c Variables 1..36 say which sites are active; neighbouring sites cannot both transmit.
c Each site has two hidden radio switches. It is active iff at least one switch is on.
c Projecting onto sites counts each feasible activation pattern once, regardless of its switches.
c Each site requests transmission independently with probability 1/5.
c The projected weighted count is the probability that no neighbours transmit together.
c Exact probability: 2525856086739112849047552/14551915228366851806640625. Hidden switch assignments contribute no extra probability.
c t pwmc
